course: dictionary
lesson: 11713
title: The auricle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one subject. Auricle is a science word, and you meet it in lessons about the ear and the heart. When you see it, look at the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «You can see the auricle on the side of your head.» The word says it is something you can see, and «side of your head» tells you where it is.
explain: The phrase «the auricle of the ear» is the one to remember. The auricle is the outer part of the ear, the part you can see. Its other name is the pinna, so if a text says pinna, it means the same thing.
explain: Auricle has an old use too. «In an old science book, the auricle was a small pouch in the top of the heart.» The clue is «in the top of the heart», so here the word names a small part inside the body, not part of the ear. Always ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Auricle is a noun. One is an auricle, and two or more are auricles.
fact: «Auricle» means the outer part of the ear that you can see, also called the pinna.
fact: In old science use, «auricle» means a small pouch-like part of the upper chambers of the heart, which are called atria.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and they can help you work out its meaning.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, the subject and the other words tell you which meaning is meant.
exercise: «Mia pulled her hat down over her auricle to keep it warm.» What is an auricle? | The tip of the nose | The part of the heart that pumps blood out | A small pouch inside the lungs | *The outer part of the ear that you can see
exercise: «The doctor pointed to the auricle on the heart diagram.» Which meaning fits this sentence best? | A bone in the knee | *A small pouch-like part of the upper chambers of the heart | A thin layer of skin on the hand | The outer part of the ear
exercise: Which other name is given for the auricle? | *Pinna | Pancreas | Pupil | Pillow
test: «Sam felt the cold wind on his auricle as he cycled to school.» Which part of Sam's body is this? | *The outer ear | The elbow | The thumb | The nose
test: In the sentence «The auricle was a small pouch in the top of the heart», what does auricle mean? | The part of the eye that lets in light | A type of muscle in the leg | A long tube in the throat | *A small pouch-like part of the upper chambers of the heart
exam: Which meaning of auricle matches the phrase «the auricle of the ear»? | A small bone deep inside the ear | The skin covering the eyelid | A pouch in the top of the heart | *The outer part of the ear that you can see
